## Additional Datasets to Improve the Project

| Dataset | What It Provides | Where to Get It |
|---------|-----------------|-----------------|
| **CrackTree260** | 260 pavement images with crack annotations, useful for secondary crack detection in temporal analysis | GitHub: fyangneil/pavement-crack-detection |
| **KITTI Stereo** | Stereo pairs with calibrated depth ground truth — enables depth model validation | kitti.is.tue.mpg.de |
| **BDD100K** | 100K diverse driving images across weather/time conditions (rain, fog, night) — fills adverse condition gap | bdd-data.berkeley.edu |
| **nuScenes** | Multi-sensor driving dataset with rain/night scenes + IMU/GPS data — provides real adverse weather images | nuscenes.org |
| **Mapillary Vistas** | 25K street-level images with fine-grained semantic segmentation across 66 countries — geographic diversity | mapillary.com/dataset |
| **LTPP (FHWA)** | Long-Term Pavement Performance database with actual distress severity ratings and longitudinal monitoring — real severity ground truth | infopave.fhwa.dot.gov |
| **SWD (Smart Water Detection)** | Road puddle/water detection dataset — directly useful for water detection module training | Various papers (Chen et al. 2020) |
| **RoadDamageDataset 2024** | Updated RDD with additional countries and more D40 samples | GitHub: sekilab/RoadDamageDetector |
| **Custom IMU Collection** | Paired camera+IMU data using STM32F429+MPU6050 — physically grounded severity labels | Self-collected per Phase 4 protocol |

**Top 3 recommendations**: (1) BDD100K for adverse weather diversity, (2) LTPP for real severity ground truth, (3) Custom IMU collection for physics-based labeling.

